/// A dependency authored in Kio' stays Kio' through materialization: the
/// library's literals carry their `(Type)` annotations spelled both ways —
/// `41(I32)` through a selective import and `42(t.I32)` through a module
/// alias — and `fmtlib.dep.kio`'s `rehost` replaces the library's own host
/// declarations with generated wrappers over `testapi/fmt` and a type
/// alias over `testapi/adapter`. The whole materialized closure parses as
/// Kio' (the case carries IS_KIO_PRIME), so the annotation's type path is
/// requalified through the re-rooted `fmtlib/types` and the case runs on
/// the kio-prime differential, where the printed value flows through the
/// alias-qualified annotation.
module testapi/main;

import fmtlib/show(show);

pub fn main() -> . { show() }
